PPA Source Package — fcitx5-skey
=================================

This directory contains the Debian packaging for fcitx5-skey, intended
for upload to Ubuntu Launchpad PPA.

Quick Start
-----------

1. Create the orig tarball (bundles skey-engine source):

    ./scripts/make-ppa-source.sh

2. Build and upload from the clean temporary tree (recommended on NixOS):

    PPA_REUSE_ORIG=1 ./scripts/ppa-build-upload.sh 0.9.3 "noble resolute"

   `ppa-build-upload.sh` extracts the `.orig.tar.gz` into a temporary
   directory before invoking `debuild`, so read-only files under a workspace
   mount such as `.cache/nixos/nix/store` are never scanned by `dh_clean`.
   Omit `PPA_REUSE_ORIG=1` only when creating a genuinely new upstream
   version. Launchpad treats an `.orig.tar.gz` filename as immutable.

   For a local source-only build, extract the orig tarball and copy `debian/`
   into that clean tree, then run `debuild -S -sa` there.

3. Check package quality:

    lintian --pedantic ../fcitx5-skey_*.changes

4. Upload to Launchpad PPA:

    dput ppa:collyn094/fcitx5-skey ../fcitx5-skey_*_source.changes

About skey-engine (Rust)
-------------------------

skey-engine is a stateless Vietnamese input method engine written in Rust.
It ships as a static library (libskey_engine.a) that links into the C++
fcitx5 addon. Its `libc` Cargo dependency is vendored into the orig tarball
so the Launchpad buildd can build it without network access.

During the build, CMake receives `-DSKEY_ENGINE_SOURCE_DIR=$(CURDIR)/skey-engine`
(via debian/rules) to use the bundled source instead of cloning from GitHub.
